abstract: >-
  The Luddite-fallacy claim about aggregate unemployment still holds in U.S. and
  Western official data through mid-2026. The Ricardo–Acemoglu–Restrepo claim
  about task displacement, labor’s share of income, and which cohorts lose the
  hiring channel is the part that is moving. Version 1.1 adds a Western
  comparison (Canada, United Kingdom, euro area, Australia) and states the
  claim as a testable identity—the Displacement–Redundancy Balance—with two
  monitoring statistics, the canary residual and the wage-fund conversion
  ratio, that later vintages can reshape.
